{number: 173}
{title: No One Ever Cared for Me Like Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I would [C] love to tell you what I think of Jesus,
Since I [G7] found in Him a friend so strong and [C] true;
I would tell you how He changed my life completely;
He did [G7] something no other friend could [C] do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No [F] one ever cared for me like [C] Jesus;
There's no [G7] other friend so kind as [C] He;
No [F] one else could take the sin and darkness [C] from me;
O how [G7] much He cared for [C] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
All my [C] life was full of sin when Jesus found me;
All my [G7] heart was full of misery and [C] woe,
Jesus placed His strong arms about me
And He [G7] led me in the way I ought to [C] go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Ev'ry [C] day He comes to me with new assurance;
More and [G7] more I understand His word of [C] love.
But I'll never know just why He came to save me,
Till someday I [G7] see His blessed face a-[C] bove.
{end_of_verse}
